ediate"><addressbook><name>TSUKAHARA, MASANORI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>The relation between the voltage Vp (kV) applied to separation electrodes and the distance L (cm) between the separation electrodes is defined by Vp/L&lt;/=10.  Even if a spark (20) is produced between the electrodes, namely, between an electrode drum (1) and an electrode plate (2), plastic pieces (3, 3') can be correctly separated with high accuracy without degrading the separation performance.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Pour cette invention, on utilise une relation entre la tension Vp (kV) appliquée aux électrodes de séparation et la distance L (cm) séparant lesdites électrodes de séparation telle que Vp/L&lt;/=10. Même lorsqu'une étincelle (20) se produit entre les électrodes, à savoir entre un tambour électrode (1) et une plaque électrode (2), des pièces plastiques (3, 3') peuvent être correctement séparées avec une précision élevée, sans nuisances pour l'opération de séparation.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>